IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-vintage`
IMPORT `je54-art01-commencement`
IMPORT `je54-art01-by-date`

-- je54-tests-crosschecks: CROSS-CHECKS.  These cases apply the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 to instruments it does not contain: the commencement dates of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (L.41/2014) and of the
-- orders that brought it into force.  They are not tests of the Interpretation Law's own text and are kept apart from the other test modules for that reason.
--
-- Provenance of the dates.  Lines 868 to 902 of the Charities source (the Table of Legislation History in its endnotes) were read and nothing else of that file.  They give: "Parts 1 to 3, Articles 32, 38, 39, 40, 42, 43
-- and 44 and the Schedules, in force 21 November 2014"; "Parts 4, 5, 7, 8 (other than Article 32), Article 37 in force 1 May 2018 (R&O.17/2018)"; "Remainder in force 1 January 2019 (R&O.17/2018)".
-- The 9.30 a.m. on 27 February 2024 case (R&O.10/2024 Article 5) is given by the brief and was NOT found in those lines.  The integrator found it in R&O.10/2024 itself on 2026-10-28 (subject je/charities-2014, source/amending/RO-010-2024.txt, lines 46 and 90: "comes into force at 9.30 a.m. on 27th February 2024").
--
-- What the lines do not give: the days on which the Law and the orders were made.  For a named-day commencement the made-day matters only to choose the text of the Law that is read (the inferred text for any made-day from
-- 28 March 2003 to 31 December 2018, V1 from 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021), so each case below is put with more than one made-day inside the range, and no made-day is asserted to be the true one.
-- R&O.10/2024 was made in 2024 (the year is in its number); both made-days used for it are in 2024 and the result does not depend on which.
--
-- Jersey is on GMT in winter and BST (UTC+1) in summer: 21 November 2014 00:00 is 21 November 00:00 UTC; 1 May 2018 00:00 is 30 April 23:00 UTC; 1 January 2019 00:00 is 1 January 00:00 UTC.

GIVETH A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
`reading a` MEANS `whether the enactment had come into force before 28 September 2021`

GIVETH A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
`reading b` MEANS `the day the enactment was passed or made`

GIVETH A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
`reading c` MEANS `the day on which the question about the enactment is asked`

`the V1 basis` MEANS `read from the deposited text in force on that day`
`the inferred basis` MEANS `inferred from the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation, not verified against L.16/2003`
`the 2021 Law basis` MEANS `governed by the 2021 Law, Article 3(2)`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      mo IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
      h IS A NUMBER
      mi IS A NUMBER
      s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
`an instant in UTC` y mo d h mi s MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (YMD y mo d) (TIME_FROM_HMS h mi s) "Etc/UTC"

GIVEN named IS A DATE
      made IS A DATE
      asked IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`an order naming the day` named `made on` made `asked about on` asked MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS `on a particular day`
        `the day it names` IS JUST named
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS asked


§ `Parts 1 to 3 and the Schedules of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: in force 21 November 2014`

#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `made on` (YMD 2014 10 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2014 11 21
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `made on` (YMD 2014 10 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the inferred basis`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `made on` (YMD 2014 10 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`)'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2014 11 21
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `made on` (YMD 2014 10 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the inferred basis`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `made on` (YMD 2014 11 21) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2014 11 21
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `made on` (YMD 2014 11 21) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the inferred basis`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `made on` (YMD 2014 11 21) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`)'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2014 11 21
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `made on` (YMD 2014 11 21) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the inferred basis`
#ASSERT DATETIME_SERIAL ((`Article 1(4) by date: the moment at which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `made on` (YMD 2014 10 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) "Europe/Jersey" `reading a`)'s `the moment`) EQUALS DATETIME_SERIAL (`an instant in UTC` 2014 11 21 0 0 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force at the instant` (`an instant in UTC` 2014 11 20 23 59 59) "Europe/Jersey" (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `made on` (YMD 2014 10 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force at the instant` (`an instant in UTC` 2014 11 21 0 0 0) "Europe/Jersey" (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `made on` (YMD 2014 10 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the answer`

