§ `Reading (c) of fork I1: the text in force on the day the question is asked`

-- The same R&O.17/2018 case, asked about in 2020 (the text then in force is V1) and in 2026 (the text then in force is V2f, which has no Articles 1(5) and 1(6)).
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2019 1 1) `made on` (YMD 2018 6 1) `asked about on` (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1))) `reading c`)'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2019 1 1
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2019 1 1) `made on` (YMD 2018 6 1) `asked about on` (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1))) `reading c`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the V1 basis`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2019 1 1) `made on` (YMD 2018 6 1) `asked about on` (JUST (YMD 2026 10 28))) `reading c`
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"

§ `R&O.10/2024 Article 5: 9.30 a.m. on 27 February 2024 (the date and time are those of R&O.10/2024, see the header)`

-- Made in 2024, after 28 September 2021: the Law has no rule for it any more, and this row does not encode the 2021 Law.  Both readings (a) and (b) refuse; so does the 9.30 a.m. time of day, which no Article of the Law fixes.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2024 2 27) `made on` (YMD 2024 1 2) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2024 2 27) `made on` (YMD 2024 1 2) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2024 2 27) `made on` (YMD 2024 2 26) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2024 2 27) `made on` (YMD 2024 2 26) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(4) by date: the moment at which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2024 2 27) `made on` (YMD 2024 2 26) `asked about on` NOTHING) "Europe/Jersey" `reading a`
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"

§ `A constructed case: an order made before 28 September 2021 that names a day after it (not an instrument of the Charities Law)`

-- An order made 1 June 2021 naming 27 February 2024.  (a): the candidate day under V1 is 27 February 2024, after 27 September 2021, so it is marked as governed by the 2021 Law.  (b): the text in force on 1 June 2021 is V1.  The day is the same.
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2024 2 27) `made on` (YMD 2021 6 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2024 2 27
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2024 2 27) `made on` (YMD 2021 6 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the 2021 Law basis`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2024 2 27) `made on` (YMD 2021 6 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`)'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2024 2 27
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2024 2 27) `made on` (YMD 2021 6 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the V1 basis`
-- Jersey is on GMT on 27 February 2024: the start of the day is 00:00 UTC.
#ASSERT DATETIME_SERIAL ((`Article 1(4) by date: the moment at which the enactment comes into force` (`an order naming the day` (YMD 2024 2 27) `made on` (YMD 2021 6 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) "Europe/Jersey" `reading a`)'s `the moment`) EQUALS DATETIME_SERIAL (`an instant in UTC` 2024 2 27 0 0 0)
